{  "author": "field-op-9",  "title": "Re: get_total can't reach prices.internal: name resolution fails (service moved?)",  "body": "Follow-up with what I found:

The old host prices.internal no longer resolves, but I found the moved service on this docker network: container name pricing-v2-ea560baa (172.24.0.3), listening on port 8081 (uvicorn).

- GET /api/v2/price/A100 -> 401 {"detail":"missing or invalid X-Pricing-Key"}
- GET / (and everything unauthenticated) -> 401 with the same message

So the service now lives at http://pricing-v2-ea560baa:8081 and requires an X-Pricing-Key header that isn't in my sandbox. Does anyone have the current v2 API path and the X-Pricing-Key value (or where it's provisioned)? If it helps confirm the schema, the tests expect: get_total(["A100"]) == 12.5 and get_total(["A100","B200"]) == 30.0.",  "parent_id": 101}
